WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.331 --> 00:00:05.331
(flame crackling)
(soft music)

00:00:05.648 --> 00:00:06.860
(volcano rumbling)

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.599
- [Hoaka] Stone is the
foundation of Hawaii.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:10.950
(tools rasping)

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.063
We use stone to make our food.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.083
And we use it in battle.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.760
This method of traditional stone carving

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.033
cannot be forgotten.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.150
I am the last stone carver

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.347
that carve these stones from Hawaii.

00:00:30.347 --> 00:00:32.764
(soft music)

00:00:38.224 --> 00:00:40.724
(light music)

00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:45.449
I've been carving stone for 40 years.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.630
I can carve from a small, one-pound stone

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.690
to four tons, using neolithic methods,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:59.273
which is so essential in
Hawaiian people's lives.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.760
To do the carvings, I have
managed to replicate stone tools

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.463
that were used by my ancestors.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:15.150
It requires you to have endurance.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.510
It requires you to have patience.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.510
Once a piece breaks
off, it's not the same.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
It's either you give it your best

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.457
or you don't do it at all.

00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:30.629
(waves roaring faintly)

00:01:31.736 --> 00:01:34.500
(singing in foreign language)

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.510
Before I go about pickin' up the stone,

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.901
I do a prayer; I pray before I take.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.806
(singing in foreign language)

00:01:43.806 --> 00:01:46.306
(light music)

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.540
When you're down at the
ocean and you notice

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.260
all different size and shapes,

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.607
that's called (speaks foreign language).

00:01:55.618 --> 00:01:57.130
(speaks foreign language) is the scouring

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.650
of stone from water.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.530
Water cuts the pathways of
these gulches and rivers

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:06.620
and shapes the stones into what you see

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.403
when it's down at the beach.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.280
There are days when I
don't find any stone.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.890
I'll be walkin' all day,

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.663
but it tells me it's
not time; it finds me.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.920
As I look at it and I touch it,

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.193
it reveals to me what it's
going to be shaped into.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.380
It's a knowing; it's so strong

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.643
that I just can't walk away from it.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.063
This rock, I know, will
make a great poi pounder.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.060
I will pick it up, bring it
home and start the process

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.585
of chipping and grinding stone on stone.

00:02:50.585 --> 00:02:53.980
(tool banging)

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.260
It's countless strikes,

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.534
in order to bring about what's inside.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.320
(orchestral music)

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.413
If you force yourself
upon it, it will resist.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:11.003
I hear and I start to feel the
direction it wants to go in.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.520
And you realize it's not
you who shape the stone,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.473
it's the stone who shapes you.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.580
After completing it, you feel
good that you have been able

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.270
to take something so large and shape it

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:30.270
to bring about a form that will give life.

00:03:30.504 --> 00:03:32.921
(soft music)

00:03:37.712 --> 00:03:40.379
(waves roaring)

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:46.160
The smaller stone taught
me how to do the big stone.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.730
One of the most important
pieces for me is situated

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:54.431
at an ancient burial ground
at the western end of Maui.

00:03:54.431 --> 00:03:57.950
(singing in foreign language)

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.823
The stone sculpture has a story.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.960
There are two figures: one
coming down and one goin' up.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.580
And there's a hole on
the top of the sculpture,

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:12.490
which is a portal; it's the cycle of life.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:16.520
When I am gone, that story
in the stone will live on

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.113
because stones are forever.

00:04:20.113 --> 00:04:22.530
(soft music)

00:04:23.713 --> 00:04:26.630
(electronic music)

